WEBVTT

00:44:28.496 --> 00:44:30.621
which I hope they don't and
don't think they will.

00:44:31.413 --> 00:44:34.746
So the way it's set up is that if at some
point in the coming year or two,

00:44:34.746 --> 00:44:39.579
two years, Microsoft decide that there's
some incredible commercial opportunity

00:44:39.871 --> 00:44:43.788
that they could realize out of the eye
that you've built and you feel actually,

00:44:43.788 --> 00:44:46.538
no, that's that's damaging. You
can block it. You can veto it.

00:44:46.829 --> 00:44:50.079
Correct. So the four most powerful
version of three

00:44:50.079 --> 00:44:52.579
and its successors are available
via the API,

00:44:52.579 --> 00:44:54.413
and we intend for that to continue.

00:44:55.204 --> 00:44:59.954
What Microsoft has is the ability to sort
of put that model directly into their

00:44:59.954 --> 00:45:01.954
own technology. If they want to do that.